# Agent skills & plugins catalog, consumed by setup/agent-skills.sh
#
# Format per line:  category|id|description|install
# A line starting with '#' is a comment. Install fields may contain spaces
# and shell operators but no '|'.
#
# Categories:
#   agents-skill    clone <git-url> and copy one skill folder into
#                   ~/.agents/skills/<id>; install field: <git-url>@<folder>
#   pi-package      pi package/extension; install field is a shell command
#   plugin          clone <git-url> and run its own installer (TUI); the plugin
#                   detects harnesses and installs per its own layout
#   agent-tool      one entry per utility (MCP/plugin/skill shipped by a third
#                   party); setup/agent-tools.sh installs it into every harness
#                   present (opencode, claude, codex, cursor, pi, kiro, ...)
#
# Skills that ship inside an installable package are agent-tool entries, not
# vendored copies: graphify (PyPI graphifyy + `graphify install`), teach &
# friends (cloned from repo into ~/.agents/skills). Only genuinely private
# skills with no public source would justify a vendored copy (setup/skills/).
#
# ~/.agents skills are harness-agnostic (AGENTS.md / .agents/skills are read
# by pi, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, kilo, ...). Orca-managed skills are
# intentionally NOT listed here.
#
# ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json is Claude's native skill-sync state. The catalog
# is the repo-owned install path; the lock file is not committed.

agents-skill|find-skills|Skill discovery & install guide|https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills.git@skills/find-skills
agents-skill|show-me|Explain topics with diagrams & HTML artifacts|https://github.com/humanlayer/skills.git@plugins/show-me/skills/show-me
agents-skill|teach|Teach a skill or concept within the workspace|https://github.com/mattpocock/skills.git@skills/productivity/teach
agents-skill|grill-me|Cross-examine plans, ideas and proposals|https://github.com/mattpocock/skills.git@skills/productivity/grill-me
agents-skill|grill-with-docs|Grill claims with real documentation evidence|https://github.com/mattpocock/skills.git@skills/engineering/grill-with-docs
agents-skill|tdd|Test-driven development workflow|https://github.com/mattpocock/skills.git@skills/engineering/tdd
agents-skill|improve-claude-md|Improve CLAUDE.md instruction adherence|https://github.com/humanlayer/skills.git@plugins/improve-claude-md/skills/improve-claude-md

agent-tool|graphify|Any input to a persistent knowledge graph (PyPI graphifyy: skill + graphify install)|setup/agent-tools.sh install graphify

# use-railway intentionally NOT listed: it ships from the official
# railwayapp/railway-skills repo (plugins/railway/skills/use-railway) —
# install it from there when wanted, not from this repo.

plugin|awesome-agent|assawalhy/awesome-agent: commands, sub-agents and skills (awesome-plan, ddd, pr-description) for every harness|https://github.com/assawalhy/awesome-agent.git

pi-package|tmustier-pi-extensions|pi-extensions: extensions & skills by tmustier (ralph loop, raw-paste, extend-pi, ...)|pi install git:github.com/tmustier/pi-extensions

# Multi-harness tools: install field is handled by setup/agent-tools.sh, which
# targets every harness present on the machine.
agent-tool|context7|Up-to-date library docs via MCP (opencode/codex/cursor/claude/pi)|setup/agent-tools.sh install context7
agent-tool|plannotator|Plan & code review: opencode/claude plugins, pi extension, codex/kiro/gemini hooks|setup/agent-tools.sh install plannotator
agent-tool|typescript-lsp|Claude Code LSP speedups (claude-only upstream)|setup/agent-tools.sh install typescript-lsp